      },
      "source": [
        "Create Groq Client"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "zgm1w4K3sWnk",
        "outputId": "693da8bd-e8aa-4987-84d0-37533d40a52b"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "openai/gpt-oss-safeguard-20b\n",
            "meta-llama/llama-prompt-guard-2-22m\n",
            "canopylabs/orpheus-v1-english\n",
            "openai/gpt-oss-20b\n",
            "openai/gpt-oss-120b\n",
            "canopylabs/orpheus-arabic-saudi\n",
            "meta-llama/llama-prompt-guard-2-86m\n",
            "allam-2-7b\n",
            "whisper-large-v3-turbo\n",
            "qwen/qwen3.8-27b\n",
            "whisper-large-v3\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from groq import Groq\n",
        "import os\n",
        "\n",
        "client = Groq(api_key=os.getenv(\"GROQ_API_KEY\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "models = client.models.list()\n",
        "\n",
        "for model in models.data:\n",
        "    print(model.id)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qftzH27qs-Uh"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Create Summarization Agent\n",
        "\n",
        "Create an agent that summarizes papers consistently."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cKDR7arPtB9F"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def summarize_paper(text):\n",
        "\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "\n",
        "        response = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
        "            model=\"openai/gpt-oss-20b\",\n",
        "            messages=[\n",
        "                {\n",
        "                    \"role\": \"system\",\n",
        "                    \"content\": \"\"\"\n",
        "                    Summarize the paper in four sections:\n",
        "\n",
        "                    1. Objective\n",
        "                    2. Methodology\n",
        "                    3. Key Findings\n",
        "                    4. Limitations\n",
        "\n",
        "                    Keep under 500 words.\n",
        "                    \"\"\"\n",
        "                },\n",
        "                {\n",
        "                    \"role\": \"user\",\n",
        "                    \"content\": text[:9000]\n",
        "                }\n",
        "            ]\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        return (\n",
        "            response\n",
        "            .choices[0]\n",
        "            .message.content\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    except Exception as e:\n",
        "\n",
        "        return f\"Summary Error: {e}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "3btUG_7ft0vr",
        "outputId": "07af343d-db9b-48b6-9880-67c68be5be4c"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Title: Exploring the Formation of Student Experience Values and Its Impact on Higher Education Satisfaction in South Sumatra, Indonesia\n",
            "\n",
            "Objective:\n",
            "The objective of this study is to analyze the means of creating positive student experiences in higher education, focusing on how increased cocreation can lead to higher experiences values and, in turn, enhance student satisfaction. The study specifically aims to explore the connections between cocreation, experience values, and student satisfaction in the context of South Sumatra universities in Indonesia.\n",
            "\n",
            "Methodology:\n",
            "The research employs a survey confirmatory approach and is conducted at 32 universities in South Sumatra Province. A total of 357 students are surveyed using a stratified random sampling technique. Data analysis utilizes structural equation modeling (SEM) to evaluate the research model and relationships between cocreation, experience values, and student satisfaction.\n",
            "\n",
            "Key Findings:\n",
            "1. Experiential values in higher education are formed through increased cocreation, with students directly participating in various campus activities. Enhanced cocreation demonstrates stronger student attachment to the institution and fosters higher experiential value.\n",
            "2. Cocreation does not directly influence student satisfaction; instead, it indirectly affects experience values, which in turn enhance student satisfaction.\n",
            "3. The study confirms that enhancing cocreation and subsequently elevating experiential values contribute to higher levels of student satisfaction.\n",
            "\n",
            "4. The findings emphasize the importance of engaging students in various campus activities to foster cocreation and develop positive experiences, which will eventually lead to higher satisfaction levels among students.\n",
            "\n",
            "Limitations:\n",
            "1. The study focuses on higher education institutions in South Sumatra, Indonesia, limiting the generalizability to other regions or countries.\n",
            "2. The data is solely based on student perceptions, which may have limitations regarding the external validity of the findings with regard to administrators, faculty, and other stakeholders.\n",
            "3. The study relies on self-reported data, prone to potential biases such as social desirability and memory limitations.\n",
            "\n",
            "4. The research does not explore the connections between cocreation, experience values, and student satisfaction in specific areas such as academics, campus environment, and social aspects, leaving opportunities for future investigations.\n",
            "\n",
            "5. Further research could examine the influence of cocreation on the institutional branding and perceived quality, as well as exploring the moderating factors that may impact the relationship between cocreation, experience values, and student satisfaction. \n",
            "\n",
            "In conclusion, this study investigates the role of cocreation in shaping higher education experiences and evaluating its correlation with experience values and student satisfaction in the South Sumatra region of Indonesia. The findings demonstrate that enhancing cocreation by involving students in various campus activities would contribute to higher satisfaction levels among students. Although the research is centered on a particular region and relies on students' perspectives, these findings can inform higher education institutions globally regarding the importance of engaging students and fostering cocreation to enhance students' experiences and overall satisfaction. Future research can focus on exploring the influence of cocreation on institutional branding and perceived quality, as well as examining the moderating factors impacting the relationship between cocreation, experience values, and student satisfaction. \n",
            "\n",
            "Implications:\n",
            "1. Higher education institutions should prioritize cocreation by involving students in campus activities to promote positive experiences and improve students' overall satisfaction.\n",
            "2. Engaging students and fostering cocreation can lead to improved perception of quality, institutional branding, and higher satisfaction levels among students.\n",
            "3. Interactions between cocreation, experience values, and student satisfaction should be examined to enhance the effectiveness of cocreation strategies.\n",
            "4. Taking into account the student perspective, higher education institutions may find it useful to tailor cocreation initiatives according to their regional contexts, considering the limitations mentioned in the study, such as the focus on South Sumatra and the students' perspective.\n",
            "5. It is crucial for institutions to integrate cocreation initiatives to promote positive experiences and satisfaction among students. While the research's geographical context may limit the generalizability of the findings, the insights gained can inspire more comprehensive studies considering institutional contexts, multiple stakeholders' perspectives, and moderation interactions between cocreation, experience values, and satisfaction.\n",
            "\n",
            "In summary, the research exhibits the critical aspects of students' involvement in campus activities as a means to boost experience values, which in turn enhances student satisfaction. While acknowledging the study's limitations, this research informs institutions on the significance of implementing cocreation initiatives, specifically in the South Sumatra region, in order to improve the educational experience and student satisfaction. Additionally, it suggests conducting more extensive studies that encompass different geographic contexts and involve various stakeholders' views as well as examining the moderating effects of cocreation, experiential values, and satisfaction relationships. \n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "print(\n",
        "    summarize_paper(\n",
        "        state.retrieved_papers[0][\"summary\"]\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "vnCCtTEryH7r"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Create Keyword Extraction Agent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Rc7f4BTXylEQ"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from collections import Counter\n",
        "import re\n",
        "\n",
        "def extract_keywords(text):\n",
        "\n",
        "    words = re.findall(\n",
        "        r\"\\b[a-zA-Z]{4,}\\b\",\n",
        "        text.lower()\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    common = Counter(words)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return [\n",
        "        keyword\n",
        "        for keyword, count\n",
        "        in common.most_common(10)\n",
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "s0NODYhqy75M",
        "outputId": "f5cf9cd2-2495-42d1-9975-585b071a8f43"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "['students',\n",
              " 'higher',\n",
              " 'student',\n",
              " 'experience',\n",
              " 'values',\n",
              " 'that',\n",
              " 'satisfaction',\n",
              " 'with',\n",
              " 'value',\n",
              " 'education']"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 21,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "extract_keywords(\n",
        "    state.retrieved_papers[0][\"summary\"]\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DYyu_v86zViM"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Create Relevance Scoring Agent\n",
        "\n",
        "Instead of assigning fixed scores, calculate them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DRSf5JNiznH1"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import (\n",
        "    TfidfVectorizer\n",
        ")\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import (\n",
        "    cosine_similarity\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "def calculate_similarity(\n",
        "    query,\n",
        "    document\n",
        "):\n",
        "\n",
        "    vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer()\n",
        "\n",
        "    vectors = vectorizer.fit_transform(\n",
        "        [query, document]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    score = cosine_similarity(\n",
        "        vectors[0],\n",
        "        vectors[1]\n",
        "    )[0][0]\n",
        "\n",
        "    return score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Ij4ZzfToz48J"
      },
      "source": [
        "Calculate Recency Score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "glrTYjr2zm1G"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from datetime import datetime\n",
        "\n",
        "def recency_score(year):\n",
        "\n",
        "    current_year = datetime.now().year\n",
        "\n",
        "    age = current_year - year\n",
        "\n",
        "    score = max(\n",
        "        0,\n",
        "        1 - (age / 10)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    return score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9dhvS09a0PXQ"
      },
      "source": [
        "Citation Score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1o1ml0HP0RD_"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def citation_score(citations):\n",
        "\n",
        "    max_citations = 1000\n",
        "\n",
        "    return min(\n",
        "        citations / max_citations,\n",
        "        1.0\n",
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "CSFCHMvA0qLV"
      },
      "source": [
        "Calculate Final Score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7CZy7weL0qxN"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def evaluate_paper(\n",
        "    paper,\n",
        "    research_question\n",
        "):\n",
        "\n",
        "    text = (\n",
        "        paper.get(\"title\",\"\")\n",
        "        + \" \"\n",
        "        + paper.get(\"summary\",\"\")\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    similarity = calculate_similarity(\n",
        "        research_question,\n",
        "        text\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    year = paper.get(\n",
        "        \"year\",\n",
        "        datetime.now().year\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    citations = paper.get(\n",
        "        \"citations\",\n",
        "        0\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    recency = recency_score(year)\n",
        "\n",
        "    citation_strength = (\n",
        "        citation_score(\n",
        "            citations\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    final_score = (\n",
        "        0.5 * similarity +\n",
        "        0.3 * recency +\n",
        "        0.2 * citation_strength\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"score\": round(\n",
        "            final_score,\n",
        "            3\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        \"reason\":\n",
        "        (\n",
        "            f\"Similarity={similarity:.2f}, \"\n",
        "            f\"Recency={recency:.2f}, \"\n",
        "            f\"Citations={citation_strength:.2f}\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fmNdKfFg1XbB"
      },
      "source": [
        "Citation Verification Agent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Hb8Luwm_1L6q"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def verify_citation(\n",
        "    paper\n",
        "):\n",
        "\n",
        "    checks = {\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"title\":\n",
        "        bool(\n",
        "            paper.get(\"title\")\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"year\":\n",
        "        bool(\n",
        "            paper.get(\"year\")\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"source\":\n",
        "        bool(\n",
        "            paper.get(\"source\")\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"url\":\n",
        "        bool(\n",
        "            paper.get(\"url\")\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    return checks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Pn6rnNrq1j4U"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Evidence Quality Agent\n",
        "\n",
        "Evidence quality should not rely only on citation count."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TSTBw-JS1Rj6"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def assess_evidence_quality(\n",
        "    paper\n",
        "):\n",
        "\n",
        "    score = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "    if paper.get(\"year\",0) >= 2022:\n",
        "        score += 1\n",
        "\n",
        "    if paper.get(\"citations\",0) > 20:\n",
        "        score += 1\n",
        "\n",
        "    if paper.get(\"doi\"):\n",
        "        score += 1\n",
        "\n",
        "    if paper.get(\"source\") == \"openalex\":\n",
        "        score += 1\n",
        "\n",
        "    levels = {\n",
        "        4:\"High\",\n",
        "        3:\"Moderate\",\n",
        "        2:\"Medium\",\n",
        "        1:\"Low\",\n",
        "        0:\"Very Low\"\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    return levels[score]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5PsUZDtz2DbI"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Create Processing Agent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1xoZXf_A2J6m"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def process_paper(\n",
        "    paper,\n",
        "    research_question\n",
        "):\n",
        "    raw_summary = paper.get(\"summary\", \"\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Bypass LLM summarization if abstract is missing or a generic placeholder\n",
        "    if not raw_summary or \"abstract not available\" in raw_summary.lower():\n",
        "        summary = f\"No abstract available. Title: {paper.get('title', '')}\"\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        summary = summarize_paper(raw_summary)\n",
        "\n",
        "    keywords = extract_keywords(\n",
        "        summary\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    evaluation = evaluate_paper(\n",
        "        paper,\n",
        "        research_question\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    citation_check = (\n",
        "        verify_citation(\n",
        "            paper\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    evidence = (\n",
        "        assess_evidence_quality(\n",
        "            paper\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    paper[\"processed_summary\"] = summary\n",
        "    paper[\"keywords\"] = keywords\n",
        "    paper[\"relevance_score\"] = evaluation[\"score\"]\n",
        "    paper[\"score_reason\"] = evaluation[\"reason\"]\n",
        "    paper[\"citation_check\"] = citation_check\n",
        "    paper[\"evidence_quality\"] = evidence\n",
        "\n",
        "    return paper"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bb2ff5c3"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Re-process all retrieved papers with our new robust process_paper function\n",
        "processed_clean = []\n",
        "for paper in state.retrieved_papers:\n",
        "    processed_clean.append(process_paper(paper, state.question))\n",
        "\n",
        "state.processed_papers = processed_clean\n",
        "\n",
        "# Re-sort by relevance score\n",
        "state.processed_papers.sort(key=lambda x: x[\"relevance_score\"], reverse=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 1000,
          "referenced_widgets": [
            "c17f674f33324f92bb518e44e96c019a",
            "7fe5e119351642c09b04db2b0b4bbc81",
            "b704973736f444f58613b1859e1e47b7",
